Greetings, fellow NetHackers,

Long-time lurker, first-time poster.

We join the saga of Brynhildr the Perenially Unlucky (Val-Hum-Fem-Neu)
at the first time she came across the only altar in about the first
twelve dungeon levels at about Dlvl 4.

She decided to make sure she was properly aligned (stethoscope
confirmed this; piously aligned), conjured forth some baddies from a
bag of tricks, meted out some finely-tuned wrath in the name of Odin
and offered up a suitably decent sacrifice in the hopes of converting
the altar.  Nothing happened except that Odin's power decreased.  So,
she spent the next 18,000 turns or so making sure she was killing
enough creatures, not pestering the big guy too often, et cetera et
cetera, all the while searching high and low for another altar.  Only
other altar was in Minetown, also to Loki.  The bastard seemed to have
a monopoly on them and was restricting the supply horribly.  Back up
she goes to Dlvl 4, (which, by this time she needed badly in order to
bless some water and possibly bring forth Mjollnir) hacks her way
through some reasonably tough randomly-generated baddies, collecting
some of the nastier corpses to offer up.

By this time I don't think she's prayed in about 10,000 turns, she
hasn't murdered anyone, broken any mirrors, attacked any peaceful
creatures or done anything that may be detrimental to her alignment or
luck.  She's also about level 12 at this point.  Here we go, I
thought.  This time we'll get it right.  So, she offers up the broken
body of the baddest enemy she's vanquished in the last few turns,
surely hoping to tip the odds in the cosmic staring contest between
Odin and Loki to her god's favour.  Still nothing.  Odin's power
decreases yet again.  So, she decides to cut her losses, and venture
farther down in the dungeon in search of a suitable altar.

Three levels onward, I move once too many, she blunders into a
floating eye and proceeds to get swarmed by a bunch of soldier ants
while frozen there.  DYWYPI?

So, there's the YASD.  The second character I've had in about a year
that has survived long enough to possibly go on the Quest and I kill
her with one tap too many on a fricking arrow key.  ARRRRRGH.

Here's my question.  Was the Random Number God just being especially
spiteful today, or do I need to do something else, like offer up a
unicorn?  I've never had a problem finding an altar of my own
alignment before, so I'm not sure what I'm missing, here.

Thanks, and happy hacking,

